{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011VkyNsCWK21oN92qAY7kER","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/memory.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Memory — struct_self_consist_ie\\\\n\\\\n## 经验教训\\\\n\\\\n### Offset hallucination\\\\nFine-tuned generative IE 模型输出正确 entity text 但 hallucinate character offsets（准确率仅 16.7%）。必须用 span realignment 后处理修复。\\\\n\\\\n### Qwen3 think block vs XGrammar\\\\nQwen3 默认输出 `<think>...</think>` 再接 JSON，但 XGrammar 强制 `{` 为第一个 token。必须在 `apply_chat_template` 中设 `enable_thinking=False`。\\\\n\\\\n### Train/inference prompt alignment\\\\n训练用 unified template \\\\\\\"Extract all structured information...\\\\\\\"，推理必须用完全一致的 template + schema hints。不对齐会导致模型不识别指令。\\\\n\\\\n### Parse failures from max_tokens truncation\\\\nmax_tokens=512 导致 3.7% parse failures。max_tokens=1024 完全消除（0/4408）。\\\\n\\\\n### submit_training_job 需要 tmux\\\\nAutoDL 5090 服务器默认无 tmux。已安装 tmux 3.2a。\\\\n\\\\n### OOM 修复：batch_size + gradient_checkpointing\\\\nQwen3-8B LoRA r=32 在 RTX 5090 32GB 上 batch_size=4 会 OOM。修复：batch_size=2 + gradient_accumulation_steps=8 + gradient_checkpointing=true。\\\\n\\\\n### vLLM 不能直接加载 LoRA adapter\\\\nvLLM 需要 merged model（有 config.json），必须先 LLaMA Factory export 合并。\\\\n\\\\n### 训练配置必须保留 best checkpoint\\\\nft_002_v2 的 best eval checkpoint 被 save_total_limit=3 删掉了。未来需 save_total_limit≥5 + load_best_model_at_end=true。\\\\n\\\\n### E1 否定乘性惩罚假说——RE SJ 问题是根本性的 (2026-05-14)\\\\n- head_sj ρ=0.210 **远低于** NER ρ_sj=0.383（Δ=-0.173）\\\\n- 每个 component 单独都比乘性组合差——乘法在帮忙不在伤害\\\\n- additive fix 无效（差 0.001）\\\\n- 根因：span-level SJ 对 RE 根本缺乏区分力，不是公式问题\\\\n- 方案 B（度量分解）排除，走方案 A（NER-primary + RE 诊断）\\\\n\\\\n### SJ vs κ 在 NER 和 RE 上表现不对称——核心发现 (2026-05-14)\\\\n- **NER**: SJ 一致显著优于 κ（p=7e-20），ρ_sj 稳定 0.36-0.39\\\\n- **RE**: SJ ρ_sj 锁死 ~0.24，模型质量和温度调参均未改善\\\\n\\\\n### T=0.7 vs T=1.0 效果 (2026-05-14, pilot_005 vs pilot_004)\\\\n- **NER**: ρ_sj 略升 0.383→0.388，无显著影响\\\\n- **RE full**: ρ_sj 反而下降 0.244→0.234（更差）\\\\n- **RE cond**: ρ_sj 显著提升 0.316→0.372（+0.056），SJ>FK 在 full set 也恢复\\\\n- RE pct_zero 几乎不变 44.3→42.4%：zero 的根因是模型能力不是温度\\\\n- Oracle headroom 收窄 16.7→13.1pp：低温牺牲多样性\\\\n- **结论**：降温对 RE full set 无帮助，RE FAIL 确认（ρ=0.234 < 0.30 硬截止线）\\\\n\\\\n### RE pct_zero 统计范围 bug (2026-05-14)\\\\nrun_mvp_pilot.py 的 `compute_sample_f1_distribution` 在 gold-empty 过滤前调用导致虚高。已修复。\\\\n\\\\n## E4 NER 多数据集泛化方案 (2026-05-14)\\\\n**推荐：SciERC + CoNLL-2003 + WNUT-17**\\\\n- CoNLL-2003：新闻域标杆，4 types，3.4K test，HF `BramVanroy/conll2003`\\\\n- WNUT-17：社交媒体+新兴实体，6 types，1.3K test，HF `leondz/wnut_17`\\\\n- 覆盖科学/新闻/社交媒体三领域，entity types 完全不同\\\\n- 需自写 BIO→UIE char-offset 转换（~50行/数据集）\\\\n- Per-dataset fine-tune（entity types 不重叠，zero-shot 不可行）\\\\n- 总工时 ~2-3 天\\\\n- 注意：原 `conll2003` HF ID 已失效，必须用 `BramVanroy/conll2003`\\\\n\\\\n## 服务器环境\\\\n- autodl-5090: 4× RTX 5090 32GB, Python 3.12, vLLM 0.18.1, LLaMA Factory 0.9.4, tmux 3.2a\\\\n- conda: /root/miniconda3/\\\\n- 环境初始化: `source /etc/network_turbo && source /root/autodl-tmp/struct_self_consist_ie/env.sh`\\\\n- 项目路径: /root/autodl-tmp/struct_self_consist_ie/\\\\n- 基座模型: /root/autodl-tmp/.hf_cache/Qwen/Qwen3-8B/\\\\n- ft_002_v2 merged (final): checkpoints/qwen3-8b-scierc-merged-v2/\\\\n- SciERC data: data/scierc/ (train.json, dev.json, test.json)\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 2793, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0171FYb22o7vwarcEdYKpY5W","session_id":"2168b128-bc29-48d5-839e-470b564c8edf","uuid":"bd41111e-7870-4960-8e6f-03deed1f7e74","timestamp":"2026-05-14T10:08:58.810Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012fJHq5TducrCE9aBY7uWVe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017ZTLCwVmMYjZrtaSRhdD2q","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R2 in a DREAM review roundtable. Your focus is **Novelty and Related Work**. Review the following paper and provide an independent, detailed review.\n\n# Paper: \"Structural Self-Consistency Enables Test-Time Scaling for Entity-Level Information Extraction\"\n\n## Paper Summary\nThe paper proposes using soft Jaccard similarity over structured IE outputs as a \"structural self-consistency\" confidence signal for test-time scaling (TTS). Sample N outputs, compute mean pairwise soft Jaccard, use it to select the best sample (best-of-N). Tests on 3 NER datasets and 1 RE dataset.\n\n## Key Claims\n- **Claim 1:** For NER, soft Jaccard ρ=0.40–0.45 with F1, outperforming Fleiss' Kappa (ρ=0.29–0.32). +3.9 F1 via best-of-16.\n- **Claim 2:** RE full-set ρ=0.27 due to compound errors, but conditional ρ recovers to 0.40.\n\n## Method\n- **Soft Jaccard (SJ):** Pairwise set similarity with partial credit for span overlap. NER: span Jaccard × type indicator. RE: head_NER_match × tail_NER_match × relation_type indicator.\n- **Confidence:** Mean pairwise SJ over C(N,2) pairs.\n- **Baseline:** Fleiss' Kappa over BIO token labels.\n- **Evaluation:** Spearman ρ between SJ confidence and instance-level F1.\n- **Best-of-N:** Select sample with highest leave-one-out mean SJ.\n\n## Related Work section covers:\n1. Self-consistency in LLM reasoning (Wang et al. 2023, majority voting)\n2. Test-time scaling (Snell et al. 2024, repeated sampling, verifiers)\n3. Confidence estimation for IE (softmax, attention entropy, calibration)\n4. Agreement metrics (Fleiss' Kappa, Jaccard/Sørensen-Dice)\n\n## Results Summary\n- 3 NER datasets (SciERC, CoNLL-2003, OntoNotes): consistent SJ > FK\n- Cross-model (Qwen3-8B, LLaMA-3.1-8B): SJ advantage holds\n- OOD: ρ degrades 13.4% but remains actionable\n- Temperature analysis: T=0.7 acts as capability filter for RE\n- RE diagnostic: per-type breakdown, capability stratification\n- Best-of-N: +3.9 F1 on SciERC NER\n- Selection curves: SJ > FK > Random across N=1-16\n\n## References (10 total):\n[1] Wang et al. 2023 - Self-consistency (ICLR)\n[2] Brown et al. 2020 - GPT-3 (NeurIPS)\n[3] Snell et al. 2024 - Scaling test-time compute (arXiv)\n[4] Lu et al. 2022 - UIE (ACL)\n[5] Luan et al. 2018 - SciERC (EMNLP)\n[6] Tjong Kim Sang & De Meulder 2003 - CoNLL-2003\n[7] Pradhan et al. 2013 - OntoNotes\n[8] Fleiss 1971 - Fleiss' Kappa\n[9] Jaccard 1912 - Jaccard index\n[10] Hu et al. 2022 - LoRA (ICLR)\n\n## Your Review Task (R2: Novelty + Related Work)\n\nEvaluate:\n1. **Novelty:** How novel is the core idea (using soft Jaccard as self-consistency signal for IE TTS)? Is it a straightforward combination of existing techniques, or does it offer genuine insight? Is the \"structural\" framing justified or is this just \"use a better metric\"?\n2. **Related work coverage:** Are important prior works missing? Specifically consider:\n   - Self-consistency beyond majority voting (e.g., Universal Self-Consistency, USC)\n   - Structured prediction confidence/calibration\n   - IE-specific TTS or multi-sample strategies\n   - Other structural similarity metrics (e.g., tree edit distance, graph matching)\n   - Verifier/reward model approaches for structured outputs\n   - Confidence estimation in NER/RE specifically\n3. **Positioning:** Does the paper adequately position itself relative to prior work? Does it overclaim novelty?\n4. **Contribution significance:** Is this a top-venue contribution? Does the diagnostic analysis (Claim 2) add sufficient depth?\n5. **Writing quality and presentation**\n\nUse a 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept.\n\nProvide:\n- Summary (2-3 sentences)\n- Strengths (bulleted)\n- Weaknesses (bulleted, with severity: minor/moderate/major)\n- Missing related work (specific papers/areas)\n- Questions for authors\n- Score and confidence (1-5)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":35997,"cache_read_input_tokens":22944,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":35997},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2168b128-bc29-48d5-839e-470b564c8edf","uuid":"f5d378da-fdaf-46d1-8593-750dfadcbdf9"}
